{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "05AY", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0004": "$\\{f_i : X_i \\to X\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0005": "$f_i^*\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{O}_{X_i}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-finite-locally-free-descends}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:707367935437be401692e5d9028881c7dfb12c71ffb99cd77d52416f4f0b135c", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e339650d1bab3ad0e132e0bb6a4f1c55f4e28bbf6c89d606a1f6ecf427ff9460", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a quasi-coherent <MATH_0003>-module.\nLet <MATH_0004> be an fpqc covering such that\neach <MATH_0005> is a finite locally free <MATH_0006>-module.\nThen <MATH_0007> is a finite locally free <MATH_0008>-module.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:69bb0c9a8e13aeb35a5676484bdac798212d34887a7ba8e6144fed3ce3a5d27b", "unit_id": "tag:05B2:statement"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "05AY", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f_i^*\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-finite-projective}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-flat-descends}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-finite-presentation-descends}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:281df540f6001f965df804dfdd548a5ebbc71daa19fc7fb70efba9cad5d57266", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:879e562999f57d880dbfa33cfac77fc0fb0ff2bb2c8ab27b20bf008a63c4b223", "source_text": "This follows from the fact that a quasi-coherent sheaf is finite locally\nfree if and only if it is of finite presentation and flat, see\nAlgebra, Lemma <REF_0001>.\nNamely, if each <MATH_0001> is flat and of finite presentation,\nthen so is <MATH_0002> by\nLemmas <REF_0002> and\n<REF_0003>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:68a1134bd4bc498194a622ada99d68113f8afb65bd5cb0ab26f9364928a7a732", "unit_id": "tag:05B2:proof"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "05AY", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{properties-section-locally-projective}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b520c5801f0722f092f13c70930512a787f0c87d8299cecff86dab95bd2d5a37", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe definition of a locally projective quasi-coherent sheaf can be found in\nProperties, Section <REF_0001>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3e2163907e271d4defd35c7a3c44c5939d04eef17dafb6fb76c81bbff3a76020", "unit_id": "tag:05AY:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "05AY", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0004": "$\\{f_i : X_i \\to X\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0005": "$f_i^*\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{O}_{X_i}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-locally-projective-descends}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:707367935437be401692e5d9028881c7dfb12c71ffb99cd77d52416f4f0b135c", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0b8af250bfae497b0ebe3c258ff2e2535d68caf934da7b790c34e98c1d75c6b1", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a quasi-coherent <MATH_0003>-module.\nLet <MATH_0004> be an fpqc covering such that\neach <MATH_0005> is a locally projective <MATH_0006>-module.\nThen <MATH_0007> is a locally projective <MATH_0008>-module.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:aadde78930e526f99961eba2d92153d97b2fcb91db5064415245d1499c8fc2d5", "unit_id": "tag:05JZ:statement"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "05AY", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{properties-lemma-locally-projective}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{algebra-theorem-ffdescent-projectivity}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:f20a547783de0936612e9b4538f83c2e603a0e8823684fafc730a9e37a01b3df", "source_text": "Omitted. For Zariski coverings this is\nProperties, Lemma <REF_0001>.\nFor the affine case this is\nAlgebra, Theorem <REF_0002>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:859304870b26219d4566bc36457ef9e3c62ebf14811ca032c6060e99fa076591", "unit_id": "tag:05JZ:proof"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "remark", "parent_tag": "05AY", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$R$", "MATH_0002": "$M$", "MATH_0003": "$R$", "MATH_0004": "$M = \\bigoplus L_n$", "MATH_0005": "$M$", "MATH_0006": "$$\nR \\longrightarrow\n\\bigoplus\\nolimits_{m \\geq 1}\n\\bigoplus\\nolimits_{(i_1, \\ldots, i_m) \\in \\mathbf{Z}^{\\oplus m}}\nL_1^{\\otimes i_1} \\otimes_R \\ldots \\otimes_R L_m^{\\otimes i_m}\n$$", "MATH_0007": "$A \\to B$", "MATH_0008": "$M$", "MATH_0009": "$A$", "MATH_0010": "$M \\otimes_A B$", "MATH_0011": "$M$", "MATH_0012": "$A$", "MATH_0013": "$A$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{examples-lemma-projective-not-locally-free}", "REF_0002": "\\cite{Bass}", "TEXTCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTOPEN_0001": "\\href{mailto:stacks.project@gmail.com}{"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{remark}\n\\label{remark-locally-free-descends}\n", "suffix": "\\end{remark}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:a505e9946f0170e8556a3ae11e725849a981a8da12831362c7e14b1e75ecfa8d", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:f8bc2cd02a044e4140a924959fd63ecc3096ab055be80546b48512b4e386298c", "source_text": "Being locally free is a property of quasi-coherent modules which\ndoes not descend in the fpqc topology. Namely, suppose that\n<MATH_0001> is a ring and that <MATH_0002> is a projective <MATH_0003>-module which is\na countable direct sum <MATH_0004> of rank 1 locally\nfree modules, but not locally free, see\nExamples, Lemma <REF_0001>.\nThen <MATH_0005> becomes free on making the faithfully flat base change\n<MATH_0006>\nBut we don't know what happens for fppf coverings. In other words,\nwe don't know the answer to the following question:\nSuppose <MATH_0007> is a faithfully\nflat ring map of finite presentation. Let <MATH_0008> be an <MATH_0009>-module\nsuch that <MATH_0010> is free. Is <MATH_0011> a locally free\n<MATH_0012>-module? It turns out that if <MATH_0013> is Noetherian, then the answer\nis yes. This follows from the results of <REF_0002>. But in general\nwe don't know the answer. If you know the answer, or have a reference,\nplease email\n<TEXTOPEN_0001>stacks.project@gmail.com<TEXTCLOSE_0001>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:dcbcb64285afc7afae7135931a5193a38a43d5ab6c4e3b706384f3d4d0cf996c", "unit_id": "tag:05VF:statement"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "05AY", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c5ebb9c4228fd4897ee52a6312dd041dafee9845948d49da8a3255de929bb2cd", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nWe also add here two results which are related to the results above, but\nare of a slightly different nature.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:aca14121c405882db0c87a5206bade899bf29e967a36f334f9f0e685931321b3", "unit_id": "tag:05AY:prose-0003"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "05AY", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0004": "$f$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0007": "$f_*\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{O}_Y$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-finite-over-finite-module}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:7f62eb9082c29c63ea62166dacb0a1f02b1dba86d1ffee3c77e4e2f2d7ecfa71", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:f54b0d02edabd10b308166d7ed8558fd4262025ab826dea49dbb10a34ae646a6", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of schemes.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a quasi-coherent <MATH_0003>-module.\nAssume <MATH_0004> is a finite morphism.\nThen <MATH_0005> is an <MATH_0006>-module of finite type\nif and only if <MATH_0007> is an <MATH_0008>-module of finite\ntype.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f8a38fe2bc2dcdb261b0a28f21bc5784319e3b5089003ab3f820469d103ab822", "unit_id": "tag:05B3:statement"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "05AY", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$\\Spec(B) \\to \\Spec(A)$", "MATH_0004": "$A \\to B$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{F} = \\widetilde{M}$", "MATH_0006": "$B$", "MATH_0007": "$M$", "MATH_0008": "$M$", "MATH_0009": "$B$", "MATH_0010": "$M$", "MATH_0011": "$A$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-finite-module-over-finite-extension}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{properties-lemma-finite-type-module}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:1c694d5f26c1c8c5cd3560bebf5062e33353028bbf636b5f521cd1c784b2baec", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:97b44cc51ae489fd145ae987c26f7fef28334d86587169d3dcfff83b17393c97", "source_text": "As <MATH_0001> is finite it is affine. This reduces us to the case where\n<MATH_0002> is the morphism <MATH_0003> given\nby a finite ring map <MATH_0004>.\nMoreover, then <MATH_0005> is the sheaf of modules\nassociated to the <MATH_0006>-module <MATH_0007>.\nNote that <MATH_0008> is finite as a <MATH_0009>-module if and only if\n<MATH_0010> is finite as an <MATH_0011>-module, see\nAlgebra, Lemma <REF_0001>.\nCombined with\nProperties, Lemma <REF_0002>\nthis proves the lemma.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:2f69864586cb6d014f928cd0a8afca1c6284ed25cb0a01d32a345e628db750f7", "unit_id": "tag:05B3:proof"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "05AY", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0004": "$f$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0007": "$f_*\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{O}_Y$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-finite-finitely-presented-module}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:7f62eb9082c29c63ea62166dacb0a1f02b1dba86d1ffee3c77e4e2f2d7ecfa71", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:cd67cc16a690b1fc368e01e8f1e126d86f119f0cb3edfc28bff27f0767021012", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of schemes.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a quasi-coherent <MATH_0003>-module.\nAssume <MATH_0004> is finite and of finite presentation.\nThen <MATH_0005> is an <MATH_0006>-module of finite presentation\nif and only if <MATH_0007> is an <MATH_0008>-module of finite\npresentation.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:62eb349a6062ede017adb1bd6ab855aa6f126fd67fa86a2ab3fc21db2c00d391", "unit_id": "tag:05B4:statement"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "05AY", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$\\Spec(B) \\to \\Spec(A)$", "MATH_0004": "$A \\to B$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{F} = \\widetilde{M}$", "MATH_0006": "$B$", "MATH_0007": "$M$", "MATH_0008": "$M$", "MATH_0009": "$B$", "MATH_0010": "$M$", "MATH_0011": "$A$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-finite-finitely-presented-extension}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{properties-lemma-finite-presentation-module}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:1c694d5f26c1c8c5cd3560bebf5062e33353028bbf636b5f521cd1c784b2baec", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6757dbe71fa89c6b2f29d5b9e499ee299532aa316616769a61b64a4bb6e15bb3", "source_text": "As <MATH_0001> is finite it is affine. This reduces us to the case where\n<MATH_0002> is the morphism <MATH_0003> given\nby a finite and finitely presented ring map <MATH_0004>.\nMoreover, then <MATH_0005> is the sheaf of modules\nassociated to the <MATH_0006>-module <MATH_0007>.\nNote that <MATH_0008> is finitely presented as a <MATH_0009>-module if and only if\n<MATH_0010> is finitely presented as an <MATH_0011>-module, see\nAlgebra, Lemma <REF_0001>.\nCombined with\nProperties, Lemma <REF_0002>\nthis proves the lemma.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:cbb9d02cac2e72b8fb8a40d0087595a7a6e387850b3012ce7e96153168be7b15", "unit_id": "tag:05B4:proof"}
